Objective: 
Find the human-readable file amongst many.

Commands used:
cd - Changes directory
ls -la - Lists all files
file ./* - Shows the file type and ./ means path to the file in this case (*), which means all files.
cat ./-file07 - Checks the insides of that file

Thought process:
Since it is in an human readable file it has to differ somehow.
So i went to the directory and checked the contents using ls. It gave me back 10 files total.
So i couldve used cat on all the files till i found the right one, but that would be inefficient.
I searched the web for a way to type the current directory path quickly and found ./   .
Now i used file ./* , since * checks all the contents inside the directory.
One of the files was ASCII and the others were data. The ASCII was the only human readable and there the password was.

